  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "Define \\(a@b = ab - b^2\\) and \\(a\\#b = a + b - ab^2.\\) What is \\[\\dfrac{6@2}{6\\#2}?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\dfrac{1}{4}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{8}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{4}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Use each operation's definition with \\(a=6\\) and \\(b=2\\), evaluating the square before multiplication:\n\\[\n6@2=6\\cdot2-2^2=12-4=8,\n\\]\n\\[\n6\\#2=6+2-6\\cdot2^2=8-24=-16.\n\\]\nThe denominator is \\(-16\\), which is nonzero, so the requested quotient is defined and equals\n\\[\n\\frac{6@2}{6\\#2}=\\frac{8}{-16}=\\boxed{-\\frac12}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
